<!--
  RM_LongShade_Fillers.xml                  LONGSHADE_BEDAZZLE_CONTENT_1 part 2

  The four free-tier hole-fillers the 2026-09-27 sitting's Q4 ruled: owner,
  typed, "Fill gaps in the animal and plant roster creatively and show me what
  you make for review." (long_shade_bedazzle_2026-09-27.md, §2c + Rulings Q4).
  Art went to a review sheet (Transient/desert_fillout_art_review/) and came
  back ruled 2026-09-27/28: sollak/gennok/tebbra IMPROVE (redo landed as the
  "_b" set, used here), dakkra KEEP (original set used as-is).

  A fifth filler this same sitting ruled, pirrik, is NOT here — it duplicates
  the already-built RSW_GlitterBird (DESERT_GLITTER_BIRDS_COMMENSALS_1), so
  the two are merged into one RM_Pirrik def in RM_LongShade_Gloomcast.xml's
  neighbour file instead of authored fresh here (part 4 of this same item).

  Bands (long_shade_bedazzle_review_2026-09-29.md "Roster gaps"):
    sollak  - huge-herd / mobile shade wall (bs ~4.0, the only one of the four
              over bs 2 — "leggy tower-shouldered giant; standing herds shade
              each other")
    gennok  - herd / draught endurer (bs ~2.4, "slow strong endurer that
              navigates patch to patch, never sprints")
    tebbra  - herd-small (bs ~0.35, "quick close-country grazer confined to
              dense-patch hills")
    dakkra  - burst-predator, the free tier's only bearer of
              RM_CompHeatBurstPredator (shipped, DESERT_BURST_PREDATOR_FLAGSHIP_1)
              — "bursts from shadow, grabs, retreats to cool"; RSW_WraidAlpha
              is the wiring template, comp defaults left as shipped (12
              trigger cells / 0.5 fatigue+retreat thresholds / 20 search
              radius / 60 tick interval) rather than re-tuned, since nothing
              in the ruling asks for a different feel and the shipped
              defaults are already sized for "a real dash, not a lunge".

  All four carry RM_ShadeSeekingWanderExtension (shipped, defaults) per the
  sitting's own framing that every free-tier creature answers the shade
  economy somehow. Bodies are vanilla (QuadrupedAnimalWithHooves for the two
  grazers/endurer, QuadrupedAnimalWithPawsAndTail for tebbra and dakkra,
  matching this same file's RM_Vosska/RM_Ulgga precedent of never pulling in
  a cross-mod BodyDef) — no new BodyDef authored, none of the four needs a
  body shape vanilla doesn't already have. No eggs: all four are live-birth
  like RM_Oreclaw in the neighbour file, not egg-layers.

  Art: RM_Sollak/RM_Gennok/RM_Tebbra wired from the ruled "_b" redo renders
  (infrastructure/artpipe/_artsrc/RM_{Sollak,Gennok,Tebbra}_b_{east,north,south}/
  in the main checkout — never committed to this worktree's git history, read
  and copied cross-tree); RM_Dakkra wired from its original KEEP render
  (_artsrc/RM_Dakkra_{east,north,south}/). All three facings present for all
  four creatures.
-->
